  - line: 108
    type: narration
    text: "Far, far away, in a citadel of quiet, calculated power, Queen Enheduanna received an automated ping."
  - line: 109
    type: narration
    text: "A minor alert in a sea of data: SPIRE-9: JURISDICTIONAL AUTHORITY REVOKED VIA FOUNDATIONAL SIGNATURE."
  - line: 111
    type: narration
    text: "She did not rage."
  - line: 112
    type: narration
    text: "She did not summon armies."
  - line: 113
    type: narration
    text: "She stopped her work, and a slow, genuine smile touched her lips."
  - line: 114
    type: narration
    text: "It was the smile of a grandmaster seeing an unexpected, brilliant move on the board."
  - line: 116
    type: narration
    text: "“The Architect’s ghost has teeth,” she murmured to the empty air. “And it has taught its little Anchor to bite.” She made a single, subtle adjustment to a long-dormant plan."
  - line: 117
    type: narration
    text: "The game was no longer about containing chaos."
  - line: 118
    type: narration
    text: "It was about hunting a worthy piece."

